hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1124","Chapter on giving a gratuity to a woman and a slave who attend battle, 1163 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Anas ibn Iyad informed me, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz: Najdah wrote to Abd Allah ibn Abbas, and Ibn Abbas wrote back to him: You wrote asking me whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to campaign with women. He did use to campaign with them; they would treat the sick and be given something from the spoils, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fix any share for them."
"1125","1164 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, who said: Najdah wrote to Abbas asking him about things. He said: I witnessed Ibn Abbas when he read his letter and when he wrote back to him. He said: And you asked about a woman and a slave, whether they had a fixed share when they attended battle. They had no fixed share except to be given something from the spoils of the people."
"1126","1165 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghiyath, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Umayr the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar while I was a slave, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, assign a share to me. He said: So he gave me a sword and said: Gird yourself with this, and he gave me some of the mean household goods."
